A||||7||Darren's 87 coupe||cross drilled rotors||||1||
Z||000000||Darren's 87 coupe||11-23-2001||12:02 AM||||Hey  I was looking to do some upgrades soon this spring.  I've seen Cross drilled rotors and vented brake systems at the fiero store.  A little pricey, but do-able, but what do they do???  what are the benefits, and do you recomend them?  I am probably going with a 4.9 v-8 this spring also, so the brakes need to stop the beast after the transplant.  would stock be ok or should i go cross drilled or vented or what?  I have no idea what any of these terms mean.  Thanks<BR>Darren<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blueman_copy_6.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Captain Midnight||11-23-2001||12:07 AM||||I can cross drill your rotors for $20.00 each, plus shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||11-23-2001||12:12 AM||||Cross drilled looks cool, but that's all. Get yourself a set of good street performance pads and make sure your braking system is working properly and you will see a significant improvement. Check out the Ogre's Cave for lots of good info on brake upgrades.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ITB 2M4||11-23-2001||12:20 AM||||Vented rotors are good, especially if you are going to use them hard for any length of time.  Cross drilled rotors are just for looks.  If anything, they will actually increase your braking distance, because they take away from the swept surface area of the rotor.  I race a 'stock' '84, and use the stock rotors with Fiero Store carbo-metallic race compound brake pads, and havn't had any problems with fade while running at Sebring and the infield at Daytona.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pheagey||11-23-2001||12:42 AM||||   If your ganna be riding your brakes hard and/or you want phat looks then cross drilled is the way to go.<BR>   When you run your brakes hard they liquifie on the surface. Cross drilled rotors will remove the liquidized parts so you then have solid brake pads agest your rotors again, thus slowing/stopping sooner.<BR>   Cross drilled is where they put holes thru the rotor. Sloted it where they added little linear grooves from the center to near the edge...<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed;<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageyfeiro<BR>"The car formaly know as, and has now reverted back to being known as, Pheagey's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000005||Darren's 87 coupe||11-23-2001||12:43 AM||||wow thanks guys, I don't give a damn about the "look" of my rotors, just want them to stop me good.  It's just a daily driver, but I do want to upgrade if you guys think it is needed for the V-8.  I am wanting to do the brakes now and have them last for quite a while.  The master cyl has been rebuilt already, as has the front calipers.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-23-2001||03:04 AM||||Best cheap brake upgrade is Archie's 10.25" setup (adapts bigger C4 corvette I belive, stock GM parts to your car)<P>The ultimate is Held Motorsports 12 or 13" 4-piston custom kits.   They are *complete* and a BOLT ON operation, though more expensive (still very competitive with any brake upgrade kits for ANY other car...)<P>With the Held kits, you will be able to stop under a new 911 Porsche.<P>PS: check my sig. I have drilled stock sized rotors on the t-top car (88) they don't do much of anything, braided lines, new slider pins, and new carbonmet pads do a HECK of a lot more.  The drilling gets you maybe .5-1%.  But it sure looks neat! (but that's about all, your money is probally far better spent elsewhere.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Darren's 87 coupe:<BR><B>wow thanks guys, I don't give a damn about the "look" of my rotors, just want them to stop me good.  It's just a daily driver, but I do want to upgrade if you guys think it is needed for the V-8.  I am wanting to do the brakes now and have them last for quite a while.  The master cyl has been rebuilt already, as has the front calipers.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||11-23-2001||07:16 AM||||vented are a def +. my 2 cents on cross drilled, Ive seen many of them crack -originating from the holes.||||reg||1
